            "explanation": "Trong ngữ cảnh đoạn 1, 'performed' đồng nghĩa với 'played'.",
            "passage": "<b>PERSPECTIVES ON MUSIC</b>\nIn recent years, enjoying traditional and modern music shows has attracted growing attention from educators and researchers alike. A recent national survey reports that while over eighty per cent of young musicians and audiences recognise the importance of musical performances, only about thirty-five per cent have <u><b>performed</b></u> these practices into their daily routines on the concert stage. Even when resources are available, many people still struggle to balance their busy schedules with the need to appreciate both folk music and modern pop.\nThe challenge lies not only in awareness but also in daily habits. Researchers note that active participants regularly engage in structured tasks that connect people from different cultures and relieve daily stress, whereas passive observers only join occasional events once or twice a year. Consistent practice requires patience and planning, but it delivers lasting rewards. Many individuals simply repeat outdated habits they observed in the past, which prevents them from experiencing how musical performances can inspire teenagers to learn traditional musical instruments.\nFortunately, attitudes are shifting rapidly. <b>[I]</b> Most respondents in the survey agreed that everyone should appreciate both folk music and modern pop, even though many admitted spending less than two hours a week on it themselves. <b>[II]</b> Progress was strongest in communities where schools and families worked together as partners. <b>[III]</b> Groups can begin by setting clear weekly goals and giving every member a practical role on the concert stage. <b>[IV]</b> Small, steady steps like these can turn a difficult challenge into a shared habit of cooperation.\nPromoting enjoying traditional and modern music shows matters for the long-term future. Young people who see young musicians and audiences model positive behaviours are likely to view these practices as normal, and <u><b>they</b></u> will carry those values into adulthood. In this way, musical performances not only connect people from different cultures and relieve daily stress today but also inspire teenagers to learn traditional musical instruments for generations to come.\n<i>(Adapted from Educational & Social Research Reports – Unit 3: Music)</i>"
