            "text": "a. To address this, schools and communities are now launching new social issues in schools and online.\nb. In the past, many people did not pay enough attention to addressing peer pressure, cyberbullying and body shaming among teens.\nc. Today, however, both students, counsellors and parents realise how important it is to stand up against bullying and support victims.\nd. As a result, everyone benefits when we work together to create a safe, empathetic and supportive school environment for all.\ne. These practical programmes help participants protect teenagers from cyberbullying, body shaming and negative peer pressure in their daily lives.",
