            "tapescript": "PART 1 – (Questions 1–10) Listen to the conversation and complete the Youth Outdoor Adventure Camp Enrolment Form.\nReceptionist: Good morning! Welcome to our desk. Since you’re registering as a temporary visitor today, I’ll take down your details for the form. Your full name is David Miller, isn’t it?\nMr David Miller: Yes, that’s right—David Miller.\nReceptionist: What’s your local street address while you’re staying in town?\nMr David Miller: I’m staying at 19 Station Road.\nReceptionist: 19 Station Road. And which suburb is that in?\nMr David Miller: It’s in the suburb of Millbrook. That’s spelled M-I-L-L-B-R-O-O-K.\nReceptionist: Thank you. And what’s the best phone number to contact you on?\nMr David Miller: My mobile number is 7741 8095.\nReceptionist: Great, 7741 8095. Please step through and Mrs Helen will assist you now.\nMrs Helen: Hello, David Miller. Let’s look at the second part of your form regarding Kayaking. How can I help?\nMr David Miller: Well, regarding skill level: it’s intermediate group, and the date was the 12th August.\nMrs Helen: I see—12th August. And what did your previous advisor or doctor suggest?\nMr David Miller: They suggested heat spray. However, right now I’m still unable to lift heavy paddles, and I’m experiencing some pain in my left shoulder at night.\nMrs Helen: That’s very common. First of all, you must stop using the rowing machine immediately. Instead, make sure you do warm-up stretches at home every day.",
