            "passage": "<b>“MƯA ĐỎ” (RED RAIN) — VIETNAM’S OSCAR SUBMISSION</b>\n“Mưa Đỏ” (Red Rain), a film portraying the 1972 Second Battle of Quang Tri <b>(51)</b> _________________ the Vietnam War, has been selected as Vietnam’s official submission for the Best International Feature Film at the Oscars. The Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism announced on Tuesday that the blockbuster, which has taken the country by storm, will compete in the <b>(52)</b> ______________ round of the 98th Academy Awards held by the U.S. Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences.\nTo choose the most suitable entry, the ministry set up a five-member council, which was chaired by Dang Tran Cuong, head of the cinema department. The film, written by author Chu Lai, is set in 1972, when revolutionary forces gained control of Quang Tri Province, the <b>(53)</b> ____________ dividing line between North and South Vietnam at the time.\nAfter just one month in theaters, “Mưa Đỏ” has attracted over 8.1 million viewers, the highest number <b>(54)</b> _________________ recorded in Vietnam’s box office history, and has earned VND710 billion (US$27 million), also setting a new national <b>(55)</b> ______________. According to producer Nguyen Thu Dung, who leads the People’s Army Cinema, the film’s performance has “far exceeded <b>(56)</b> ____________.”\n<b>(57)</b> _________________ by Dang Thai Huyen, the movie features large-scale sets and dramatic battle scenes, which required massive preparation. <b>(58)</b> ______________ the exact budget has not been revealed, experts believe the cost ran into several million U.S. dollars. To recreate the historical setting, the crew built a 50-hectare <b>(59)</b> _____________ along the Thach Han River in Quang Tri Province.\nThe 98th Oscar Awards will take place on March 15, 2026. Meanwhile, the shortlist for the Best International Feature category will be announced on December 16, and the final five <b>(60)</b> ______________ will be revealed on January 22nd.\n<i>(Adapted from https://e.vnexpress.net)</i>"
